  "details": "If I've made ten variations on a sound, and I want my avatar to play a different one each time the animation triggers, currently I need to set up ten separate AudioSources, even though I've specifically made it so that only one can ever be playing at a time.   This is a big hit to performance rank for nothing, which could be avoided if there were a way to *change* which clip is assigned to a *single* AudioSource instead, like we can with changing materials on a mesh.\n\nI understand that Unity itself apparently doesn't have a way for animations to do this to AudioSources the way it can with materials, but this is something that could be handled with a special component, doing something like holding a list of audioclips, and an integer property that IS controllable from animations, which would cause the component to assign a new clip when it's changed.",
